.TH GOBAN-SOAK 1 "August 2026" "GoBan 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
goban-soak \- collect long-running GoBan release evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goban-soak start
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B goban-soak status --run
.I DIR
.br
.B goban-soak report --run
.I DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B goban-soak
samples the local GoBan control API, source health, rule counters, active
bans, memory use, goroutine count, and doctor state. It stores JSON-lines
samples and produces machine-readable and Markdown reports.
.PP
The default start mode detaches. Use
.B --foreground
for service managers and CI. Reload and kernel-probe exercises are disabled
unless explicitly requested.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --duration " DURATION"
Total soak duration. Default: 168h.
.TP
.BI --interval " DURATION"
Sampling interval. Default: 10s.
.TP
.BI --sock " PATH"
GoBan daemon Unix socket.
.TP
.BI --out " DIR"
Run directory.
.TP
.B --foreground
Run without detaching.
.TP
.BI --reload-every " DURATION"
Periodically exercise transactional reload.
.TP
.BI --probe-every " DURATION"
Periodically run doctor with a temporary kernel set probe.
.SH FILES
A run directory contains run.json, samples.jsonl, runner.log, report.json,
and report.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR goban-client (1),
.BR goban-daemon (8)
